<p>A rapidly widening Middle East conflict spread further on Monday as Israel struck Beirut’s southern suburbs and other parts of Lebanon after Hezbollah launched rockets, missiles and drones toward Israel. Hezbollah said its attack was retaliation tied to the killing of Iran’s Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei. Lebanon’s Health Ministry said about 31 people were killed in the Israeli strikes. U.S. and Israeli forces also kept up strikes inside Iran, hitting ballistic missile sites and other military targets around Tehran, as Iran fired retaliatory missiles and drones at Israel and also struck U.S. Gulf allies, according to multiple reports. The pace of fighting intensified after U.S.-Israeli strikes on Feb. 28 killed Khamenei and other senior Iranian figures. President Donald Trump signaled he is open to talks with Iran’s new leadership even as he suggested the campaign could continue for weeks. That mix of pressure and diplomacy is being watched closely by regional governments focused on protecting hard-won economic stability.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OM3lZL-yHP9NL3UaJmAUi54ttqbvMgEoV6JT0sqspvcWTO_ASmaJD5dicfHSwVoMv6oS1xMcVI0uimWOkUy-O5R7T3EqT6XBdEU-cRDV27oDm8s5SlqjLYVa05DydLP4h2cJUJPJhjzXosDfPrDw8YavRxQdRh1gogU4uPtBZiVKT37QGVoaszNaQgBtq9YcVgUtby_U1MeHcEAX0cF-RpXaP2vNYSP7BN92dsdzBdq1juRIuwaxldS64037PqrlNEoPiynJNvQvxcyGEg' alt='Smoke plumes rise following missile strikes in Tehran on March 1, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Iran’s governance: After Khamenei’s death, an interim committee took over running Iran, with no clear successor publicly lined up, according to Semafor’s reporting.</li><li>Gulf spillover: Bahrain said it intercepted 61 missiles and 34 attack drones and reported one person killed by shrapnel from an intercepted missile — its first reported fatality in the war.</li><li>Retaliation pattern: The Financial Times described Iran’s newer approach as sustained barrages toward Israel paired with strikes on civilian-linked sites around the Gulf.</li><li>Intelligence role: CBS News and The New York Times reported that CIA intelligence and U.S.-Israel intelligence sharing helped pinpoint Iranian leaders ahead of the strike that killed Khamenei.</li><li>Market jitters: The Globe and Mail reported that the widening conflict and rising instability have rattled markets amid intensified attacks and new missile waves.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said he is open to talks with Iran’s new leadership, even as he signaled the U.S.-Israeli assault could continue for weeks, according to reporting. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-and-israel-pound-targets-across-iran-as-trump-signals-openness-to-talk-to-new-leadership'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: Hezbollah said it fired missiles and drones toward Israel in retaliation for Khamenei’s killing, and framed the attack as defending Lebanon and its people, according to Reuters-backed reporting. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israeli-military-launches-strikes-against-hezbollah-after-group-attacks-israel'>Al-Monitor (Reuters)</a>)</li><li>Israel Defense Forces: Israel’s military said it began striking Hezbollah targets across Lebanon after projectiles were fired from Lebanese territory, and again described Hezbollah as a terrorist organisation. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israel-hits-lebanon-after-hezbollah-fire-expanding-iran-war'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iranians (mixed reactions): Reports described sharply different reactions among Iranians, with some celebrating Khamenei’s death and others mourning and worrying about what comes next. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/khamenei-s-death-never-thought-i-would-see-this-day/a-76175776'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-and-israel-pound-targets-across-iran-as-trump-signals-openness-to-talk-to-new-leadership'>U.S. and Israel pound target